  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Judges identifies bee honey. Deut 8:8 names honey with the produce of the land without saying how it was made. Arabic dibs shows that the related term can denote fruit syrup elsewhere. The hump and the place Dabbesheth share one index key. Neither passage connects them to honey. The name Idbash occurs only in a genealogy. The Syriac noun is SEDRA lexeme 653."
